efault":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-05-24T14:16:37Z","updated_at":"2025-08-05T17:15:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in Godot v4.4.1.stable.mono\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable.mono - Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS 24.04 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11300H @ 3.10GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nSome time ago, my Godot editor suddenly started to take 2-3 minutes to load any project, where as it originally takes only ~10 seconds. After some investigation, I discovered that it was caused by a symlink in my user font folder: inside my ```~/.local/share/fonts```, there is a symlink folder \"fonts\" which links back to ```~/.local/share/fonts```, creating a looping directory. I don't know why the symlink exists. Just reporting in case someone else have this problem.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn a terminal:\n1. ```cd ~/.local/share/fonts```\n2. ```ln -svni ../fonts```\n3. Open Godot editor then load any project or start a new project. It would take much longer to load.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh"